Licensed CC-BY-4.0. No NVIDIA weights are downloaded by Nexus.

The files are listed in nexus/voice/store.py, downloaded separately after user
confirmation, and checked against pinned sizes and SHA-256 hashes. They are not
included in the Nexus distribution.

Photon runtime
The optional `voice` extra installs Moondream's `moondream` package, which
depends on Kestrel and its native kernel packages. Those runtime packages are
installed from PyPI under their own terms; Nexus does not redistribute them.
The reviewed runtime is exactly moondream 2.6.1 with kestrel 0.9.1; the worker
fails closed on any other distribution version. `kestrel-kernels` carries a
proprietary M87 Labs license and Kestrel enables basic usage telemetry by
default. Nexus therefore runs STT in an isolated worker with Hugging Face
offline, Kestrel's telemetry reporter disabled, and a best-effort Python-level
socket guard for non-loopback DNS and connections. Native runtime libraries are
not sandboxed and can bypass Python socket hooks. Review the runtime licenses,
including any separate agreement required by the proprietary kernels, before
enabling the voice extra.
